bug_report:
[9 Regression] ICE with __builtin_expect_with_probability
void bar (void);

void
foo (int i, double d)
{
  if (__builtin_expect_with_probability (i, 0, d))
    bar ();
}

ICEs at -O2:
internal compiler error: tree check: expected real_cst, have mult_expr in expr_expected_value_1, at predict.c:2471
in both C and C++.
Either we need to early (+ in documentation) require that the last argument is a floating point constant (e.g. in builtins.c folding error on the last arg not being a REAL_CST), or we need to document what it means if the last argument is a variable, whether we ignore the hint altogether or what else we do.
